## Context

Author ruling 2026-10-31: data locations are a host concern, not a project's.
Each host declares them once in `~/.config/environment.d/50-datasets.conf`,
organised by lifecycle (frozen dataset, live mirror, cache, project data):

- `DATASETS_DIR`: padme `/data/datasets`, doudou `/home/haduong/data/datasets`
  (`ours/` = data we produce, `external/` = third-party frozen)
- `MIRRORS_DIR`: padme `/data/mirrors` only; the RePEc mirror was removed from
  doudou 2026-10-31 (a work laptop keeps no mirror)

Both files were installed 2026-10-31. Layout explanations: doudou
`~/data/README.md` (installed), padme `/data/README.md` (author installs, root
dir); sources `conception/2026-10-31-data-layout-{padme,doudou}.md`. Evidence:
`conception/2026-10-31-data-access-sweep.md` (read-only sweep of 46 padme and
64 doudou repos, all positive controls fired; partly overtaken by cadens 0049,
which landed during the sweep). Models, caches, DVC, project working data,
padme-traces and arena storage stay out of scope (sweep § NOT move).

Children (one PR each, in their own repository):
- harness 1402: `transcript_spool.py` reads `DATASETS_DIR`, no directory probe;
  doudou push built from it
- archiveCIRED 0043 (PR archiveCIRED#63): archive path from `DATASETS_DIR`
- climate-finance-het 2723 (PR climate-finance-het#2002): RePEc via
  `MIRRORS_DIR`, ISTEX via `DATASETS_DIR`
- cadens 0050 (PR cadens#61): remove legacy `CADENS_RAW_DIR` leftovers

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All four children closed in their repositories
- [ ] padme `/data/README.md` installed and the empty
      `/data/datasets/external/RePEc` removed (author, sudo)
- [ ] A final sweep with the same positive controls finds no hardcoded
      `datasets/` or `mirrors/` root in EXEC or CONFIG sites
